valence_lowq_va: the EXACT-SPAN variant VA -- the span BOTH codes hold at FULL RANK (N=118 on the
MnO 2-f.u. magnetic cell), and the basis of the doc/Benchmark.md MnO rows.  It is valence_lowq_sph.bsd
minus THREE diffuse shells: Mn d 0.18, O s 0.15, O p 0.18.  Its CP2K counterpart is the
VALENCE-LOWQ-VA (Mn) + VALENCE-LOWQ-VB (O) pair in IntegrationTests/CP2K/VALENCE-LOWQ-BASIS, used by
mno_{afm2,fm}_gpw_va.inp -- function for function the same span, which is what makes the code-vs-code
offset (doc/OpenWork.md step 5) an operator statement rather than a basis statement.
SPHERICAL-d ARMS ONLY, exactly as its parent (under Cartesian d the 8 d contaminants reproduce the
rank deficiency the trim exists to avoid).
WHY IT IS A FILE.  It was previously produced by doc/scripts/bisect_valence_sph.py OVERWRITING the
committed valence_lowq_sph.bsd in the working tree, so the span a run used was invisible in the run
and unreproducible after the fact -- a benchmark row cannot rest on that.  The variants are now
first-class basis sets the user selects (GPW_BASIS_SPAN=va), and the bisect script keeps its role as
the EXPLORATORY probe generator.

!
